{
  "id": "pokemon-daisuki-club-action-points",
  "name": "Pokémon Daisuki Club Action Points",
  "category": "program",
  "description": {
    "text": "PCG Action Points (PCGアクションポイント) were the points system of the Pokémon Daisuki Club: members earned them by taking their club card to official events such as Gym Challenge and Challenge Hiroba, and each rank brought its prize by post. Gold Rank, at 1,200 points, brought Pikachu 016/DPt-P, and Super Rank, at 3,200, Cresselia 045/DPt-P and Darkrai 046/DPt-P, a pair whose Poké-Bodies work only with the other in play.\n\nWhen the L-P promos took over, Gold Rank brought Pikachu 019/L-P instead and Super Rank Cresselia 020/L-P and Darkrai 021/L-P. Above them came Hyper Rank, added in 2009, with Raichu 044/L-P at 5,200 points, Special Rank with Espeon 053/L-P and Umbreon 054/L-P at 7,200, and Master Rank, the top, with Master's Scroll 055/L-P at 8,600. The L-P Pokémon came packed with holo basic Energies: Lightning Energy 014/L-P with Pikachu and Raichu, Psychic and Darkness Energy 015 and 017/L-P with Cresselia and Darkrai and with Espeon and Umbreon.\n\nThe club card's service ended on 31 August 2010. Points earned until then still counted, and members who had reached Silver Rank or higher were sent the prize of the rank above their own by 15 October 2010.",
